// The co-op session (engine content kind `net`, id `default`): two players, the host's hero and
// one guest. A joining player's body is this prefab, at the hero's side; the engine gives it
// `PlayerId(1)` and takes the keyboard and camera marks away (they are the host's).
//
// `--stand 1` plays both in one process (a test stand with a `shards` port each);
// `--host 0` and `--join ADDR` on two machines. Everything else (send rate, interest radius,
// timeouts) keeps the engine's defaults: see `NetDef` in shards_net.
{
    "default": (
        max_players: 2,
        player_prefab: "hero",
    ),
}
